From a5f525303df3242880ef0fb5066bf18438f691bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grigory Evko <grigory@evko.io>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 07:17:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] diagnostics, c++: give the C++ context of a diagnostic to
 SARIF output

The C++ front end prints the context of a diagnostic only to the text
sink: the function line, the instantiation chain, the constexpr calls,
the constraint chain and the macro expansion trace.  A SARIF log has
none of these lines.  A reader of the SARIF log cannot see why a
constraint is not satisfied, or which instantiation caused an error.

A new callback of the diagnostic context collects the context lines
when a sink other than the text sink is active.  The C++ front end
gives each context printer one output object, which prints to the
text sink or adds a line to a list.  The SARIF sink writes each line
as a related location with its message and these properties: its kind
("gcc/context"), the diagnostic that owns it ("gcc/contextOf") and its
place before or after that diagnostic ("gcc/placement").

A related location of a nested diagnostic has no level, so the SARIF
sink also gives each nested diagnostic its kind ("gcc/kind") and its
option ("gcc/option").  Each result, each nested diagnostic and each
context line also gets the location that the text output prints
("gcc/textLocation").

When an internal error follows an error, GCC prints "confused by
earlier errors, bailing out" and exits.  That path did not finish the
sinks, so a SARIF file stayed empty.  It now finishes them, as the
paths for an internal error and for a fatal error do.

When a C family front end reads a precompiled header, gt_pch_restore
replaces line_table.  The SARIF sink and the HTML sink kept the line
maps that they were created with, and the include chain of the first
SARIF location after the read used freed memory.  The compiler
crashed, and after an error the crash took the "confused by earlier
errors" path with no result in the log.  c_common_read_pch now gives
the new line maps to each sink.

The text output does not change.  When a text sink is active, only
the text sink updates the state of the context printers.

